  "tagline": "Serverless peer-to-peer database on IPFS and libp2p using Merkle-CRDT logs.",
  "description": "OrbitDB is a peer-to-peer database for JavaScript built on IPFS (Helia) and libp2p. Every database is an append-only, content-addressed operation log replicated between peers as a Merkle-CRDT, with higher-level types layered on top: event logs, documents and key-value stores, guarded by pluggable access controllers. Peers sync whenever they connect, so apps work offline and need no central server. It is the most established option for decentralised web3-style apps. Throughput, discovery and pinning are harder than with a server database, and the community is small.",
